  That's a good argument for *not* playing early wizards as
offensive spellcasters.

>  Spell friendly armor isn't too hard to find. 

  Still harder to find than spell-hostile armor.  A +2 Dwarven 
shield kills spell-casting but makes an early wizard much more
survivable.   I've also found a +4 Elven shield, which you had 
better believe I wore. (Especially since it can be worn/removed 
in one turn for spell-casting.)

  Get a lot of +1 accessory armor (boots, helm, gloves, shield)
and then (studded) leather armor is feasible from both a 
spell-casting *and* AC viewpoint.

  Which is another reason to check spell-hostile body armor for
enchantment.  In the game where I found +4 elven mithril, melee
spell-casting was abandoned for a long time. 


  Something most players don't seem aware of is the threshold
effect of negative AC.  Once your armor class is below zero you
start taking less damage from each hit, as well as getting hit
fewer times.  (Note that this effect can make casting the spell
of protection reasonable at AC of 1 or so.)  

  Probably the big reason an early wizard should be on The Quest
for Better AC.

