  Remember that being "very fast" from Haste Self give you:

  2/3 faster Mana regen.
  2/3 faster Hp regen.

  Move or hit 2/3 faster.


  I wouldn't be surprised if the 2/3 faster Mana regen means you
have just as much Mana for offensive spells as if you *weren't*
casting "Haste Self".


  The 2/3 faster Hp regen is the equivalent of 50% more Hp.


  Remember too that you don't generate more Mana if you're at 
Max Pw.  So stop and cast a pump-up-able spell (Haste self,
detect monster, Confuse monster, Protection, or just something 
you want to practice like Light or Detect Food) when you're
at your Pw Max.




